WEBVTT

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:19.500
Before Pearson was killed, 
he dueled against someone.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.420
We now know the opponent's card.

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:25.830
I thought you might know something, Bolger.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:30.200
You know something!

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:33.710
Tell me!  Who killed Pearson?

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:35.350
Bolger!

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.420
If you want to know so badly, I'll tell you.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.990
But only if you defeat me in a duel!

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.240
A duel?

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:49.730
That's right.  If you can 
defeat me, I'll tell you.

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:55.970
But if I win, I get your Black-Winged Dragon.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.010
Due to Sirocco the Dawn's effect,

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:01.700
I can concentrate the Blackwings' 
power on Bora the Spear!

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:07.910
Good!  It has more than the 
opponent's 2000 defense points!

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.640
Not good enough, Crow.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:12.920
I activate the Continuous Trap Whiteout!

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:21.930
Whiteout negates all effects that 
your monsters give to other monsters!

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:30.810
Each individual monster isn't dangerous, but 
they create power by calling for their teammates.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:33.370
That bond is the Blackwing 
deck's special feature.

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:36.100
So I will sever that bond!

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.340
Now your Blackwings are isolated.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:46.550
As long as Whiteout is active, Blackwings 
can't rely on their teammates nor give them power!

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:52.180
He uses Whiteout to sever the monsters' 
bond, and he uses Sacred Arrow to deal damage.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:56.020
This is an anti-Blackwing deck!

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:22.350
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:27.890
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:32.470
Don't look back and keep going

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:38.130
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:43.170
There's no need to fear

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:50.810
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:56.950
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:02:57.350 --> 00:03:02.590
Streak to the infinite future

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:08.180
Dreams surpass their limits

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:16.100
And will lead you to a bright place

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:47.830
Take Flight!Black-Winged Dragon!!

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.700
Bring it, Crow!  It's your turn!

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:55.350
My turn!

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.110
This is bad.

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:01.010
If things don't change, I 
can't use Blackwings' effects.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:05.480
I have to do something about that 
Continuous Trap Whiteout first.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.950
So I won't hesitate to use this card.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:09.920
I set one card!

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:16.280
Then I summon the Tuner Monster Blackwing - 
Mistral the Silver Shield in defense position!

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:17.630
I end my turn!

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.630
My turn.

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:26.000
I summon the Tuner Monster White 
Warrior - Snow the Rope Dart.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:34.640
This card gains 100 attack points 
for every card on the field.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.920
There are seven cards on the field.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.950
Therefore, it gains 700 attack points.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.200
Snow the Rope Dart can attack you directly!

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:44.920
Go!

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:52.030
Crow!

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:59.200
Since the direct attack was successful, White 
Warrior - Fog the Treasure Shield's effect activates.

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:02.440
One of your spell or trap cards is destroyed.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.410
Do it, Fog the Treasure Shield!

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:10.650
Trap Stun was destroyed!

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:14.150
You didn't think I would notice, Crow?

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:17.120
How many times have we dueled?

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:22.460
This duel is between two people 
who know each others' strategies.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:23.920
I end my turn.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:25.860
My turn!

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:32.470
I summon Blackwing - Shura the Blue Flame!

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:38.650
Level 2 Mistral the Silver Shield 
tunes Level 4 Shura the Blue Flame!

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:44.810
Dark power, infuse the gigantic 
wings to create a divine wind!

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:46.280
Synchro Summon!

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:50.720
Rage, Blackwing Armed Wing!

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.690
Good!  He successfully Synchro Summoned!

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.990
Armed Wing attacks Snow the Rope Dart!

00:05:58.240 --> 00:05:59.690
Black Charge!

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.490
I activate my monster's effect!

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:05.700
When Snow the Rope Dart is the attack 
target, it returns to my hand.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.400
In that case, I'll attack 
Fog the Treasure Shield!

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:15.110
When Armed Wing attacks a monster in defense 
position, it gains 500 attack points!

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:24.270
If Armed Wing's attack points are 
greater than your defense points,

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:25.850
you take the difference as damage!

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:32.190
The Tuner avoided destruction, but 
he still destroyed one monster.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:34.840
Since he destroyed a monster,

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:39.760
Sacred Arrow's effect will deals 400 
points of damage at the End Phase.

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:42.370
I set one card and end my turn.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:52.480
Bolger, I can't afford to lose this duel!

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:56.460
In order to find out who killed Pearson!

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:03.130
I see.  You're very determined.

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:05.040
Then I'll show you!

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:06.660
My turn!

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:11.770
I summon White Warrior - 
Snow the Rope Dart again!

00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:16.910
Level 4 White Warrior - Snow the Rope Dart

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:19.580
tunes Level 4 White Warrior 
- Hail the Iron Hammer!

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:27.910
Born from the heart's darkness, 
descend in exchange for my soul!

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:30.350
Synchro Summon!

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:34.150
Pulse, Crimson Mefist!

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:38.020
Crimson Mefist?

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:40.030
Crimson Mefist?

00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:41.720
Why does he have that?

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:48.400
Bolger, why do you have that card?

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:52.600
No way!  Did you kill Pearson?

00:07:55.020 --> 00:08:00.790
Why?  You admired Pearson!

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:03.050
To build D-Wheels, of course.

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:04.780
D-Wheels?

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:09.320
That's right.  As you already 
know, that was our dream.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:13.530
D-Wheel development stopped 
due to lack of money.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:17.990
But one day, a rich man from the City came

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:20.960
and offered a large sum of money.

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:23.200
Offered money?

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.130
But he refused!

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:31.870
That's right.  To finish building the 
D-Wheel wasn't what was important to him.

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:37.020
It was to leave his name as 
Satellite's first D-Wheel developer!

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:39.880
He couldn't allow it!

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:44.080
In the end, he couldn't allow City 
people to snatch away his achievement!

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:45.860
That's why I...

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:47.870
Bolger!

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:51.070
Pearson, I'm taking the blueprints.

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:54.780
If you want to stop me, then defeat me!

00:08:57.630 --> 00:08:59.870
I don't regret what I did!

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:05.180
D-Wheel mass production was only 
achieved because I defeated him!

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:09.560
Former Satellite citizens 
can now enjoy Riding Duels.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.840
I was able to make D-Wheels for them.

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:16.820
Even if I'm labeled a killer, 
I'll protect the factory!

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:21.290
If you understand, hand 
over Black-Winged Dragon!

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:27.260
Along with Blackbird, I know that 
Pearson gave you Black-Winged Dragon!

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:34.570
Give me Black-Winged Dragon!

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:35.690
Now!

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:38.650
I don't believe you.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:43.380
I don't believe that Pearson was like that!

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:50.160
Then I must acquire Black-Winged 
Dragon by defeating you in this duel.

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:53.850
Even if that means you'll 
end up the same as Pearson!

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:56.590
I activate Crimson Mefist's effect!

00:09:56.590 --> 00:10:02.560
Once per turn, you take 300 points of 
damage for every card on your field!

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:03.390
What?

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:06.730
Crow!

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:12.600
Then Crimson Mefist attacks Armed Wing!

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:14.140
Cursed Blood!

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:21.880
What?

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:25.020
Is he taking real damage?

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:28.480
I'm feeling pain?

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:30.620
My body feels like it's being torn apart.

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:33.790
This is...

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:35.990
Crimson Mefist's power!

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:39.930
Sacred Arrow's effect activates 
at the end of my turn.

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:48.590
Crow, you still have time to surrender!

00:10:48.590 --> 00:10:51.840
It's not worth risking your 
life for someone like Pearson!

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:54.250
I'll never surrender!

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:57.280
I believe in Pearson!

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:13.000
My turn!

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:16.630
I activate Speed World 2's effect!

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:22.260
I remove seven Speed Counters 
to draw one card from my deck!

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:23.740
All right!

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:29.030
I summon the Tuner Monster Blackwing - 
Kochi the Daybreak in defense position!

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:33.550
I set one card-

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:36.750
At this moment, Crimson 
Mefist's effect activates!

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:42.120
When you set a spell or trap card, 
you take 300 points of damage!

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:51.430
That was so much power 
that it damaged Blackbird!

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:54.270
Crow can't physically take much more of this!

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:57.740
Crow, give up or you'll die!

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:00.790
Then try.

00:12:00.790 --> 00:12:01.710
I end my turn!

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:05.390
I see.  Then I have no choice.

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:07.030
My turn!

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:13.690
Due to Crimson Mefist's effect, you take 300 
points of damage for every card on your field.

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:16.590
That's a total of 900 points of damage!

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:18.860
Crow!

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:21.820
I activate my trap Down Burst!

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:27.630
All faceup spell and trap cards 
on your field become set!

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:29.540
What?

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:31.240
I activate another trap!

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:33.720
Delta Crow - Anti Reverse!

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:38.710
When a Blackwing monster 
on my field is faceup,

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:43.920
all set spell and trap cards 
on your field are destroyed!

00:12:44.170 --> 00:12:46.520
I have two fewer cards!

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:48.390
The damage decreases to 300 points!

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:55.680
Good.

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:59.500
By destroying Whiteout, the bond 
between Blackwings is restored.

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:04.300
You're surviving, but your life 
is like a candle in the wind.

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:08.210
I summon White Warrior - 
Sleet the Morning Star!

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:16.030
By releasing this card, when 
Crimson Mefist destroys a monster,

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:18.880
you take damage equal to 
half its attack points.

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:25.560
That means if a monster is destroyed, Crow 
takes 1400 points of damage and loses!

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:29.430
Crimson Mefist attacks Kochi the Daybreak!

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:31.030
Cursed Blood!

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:32.230
Crow!

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:37.230
By sending Blackwing - Jetstream the Blue 
Sky from my hand to the graveyard...

00:13:37.530 --> 00:13:41.570
I can negate the destruction 
of one Blackwing monster!

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:43.420
What?

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:44.780
He managed to dodge it.

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:47.380
But it'll be over next turn.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.750
I set one card and end my turn.

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:50.970
Damn.

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:54.890
If I set a card, I'll take damage, 
and my life points will become 0.

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:57.800
Is it impossible to defeat Crimson Mefist?

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:00.150
Crow.

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:01.460
Over here!

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:06.300
Crow, can you hear me?

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:07.960
We're with you.

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:13.100
Do your best, Crow!

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:15.070
Everyone...

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:19.480
Crow, you're continuing 
Pearson's legacy wonderfully.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:21.630
Me?

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:23.110
Crow!

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:26.380
Crow, hurry up and come over here!

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:29.130
Look at the smiles on their faces.

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:33.690
You're the one who gave them smiles of hope.

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:36.290
Crow!

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:43.000
I want to protect their 
hopes and Pearson's legacy!

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:46.400
The mark of the Crimson Dragon!

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:53.340
That card!

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:56.040
What's this?

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:57.670
What's going on?

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:00.210
Black-Winged Dragon?

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:05.100
Take care of the kids, Crow.

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:09.770
I get it.

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:13.110
That's why Pearson refused the money!

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:19.170
Pearson, I understand how you felt!

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:21.030
My turn!

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:26.780
I summon Blackwing - Bora the Spear!

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:32.470
Level 4 Kochi the Daybreak 
tunes Level 4 Bora the Spear!

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:38.750
Black whirlwind, your secret 
thoughts appear on your wings!

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:41.190
Synchro Summon!

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:47.830
Take flight, Black-Winged Dragon!

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:51.130
The mark!

00:15:51.390 --> 00:15:52.330
Can it be?

00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:54.900
That's the Signer's fifth dragon!

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:06.210
Black-Winged Dragon finally appeared!

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:08.110
But this battle is already over.

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:11.300
I activate the trap Synchro Rivalry!

00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:15.320
When you Special Summon a Synchro Monster,

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:18.590
my monsters can't be destroyed 
in battle that turn!

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:21.790
I activate Speed Spell - Angel Baton!

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:26.460
When I have two or more Speed Counters, 
I draw two cards from my deck!

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:29.070
Then I send one card in 
my hand to the graveyard!

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:34.510
I send Blackwing - Zephyros the Elite 
to the graveyard and set one card!

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:38.980
If you do that, you'll take damage 
from Crimson Mefist and lose!

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:41.450
Crimson Mefist's effect activates!

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:47.250
When you set a spell or trap card, 
you take 300 points of damage!

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:49.920
Crow!

00:16:51.430 --> 00:16:55.030
Look at Black-Winged Dragon's effect!

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:56.760
What?

00:16:57.040 --> 00:16:58.260
Damage Drain!

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:01.020
When I take non-battle damage,

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:06.900
I lower Black-Winged Dragon's attack 
points by the same amount to negate it!

00:17:07.240 --> 00:17:09.940
What?  Negate damage?

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:19.280
By taking 400 points of damage and returning 
a card on my field to my hand...

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:21.590
I can Special Summon Zephyros 
the Elite from my graveyard!

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:27.460
But due to Black-Winged Dragon's 
effect, I negate that damage!

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:29.560
It lost more attack points!

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.390
What are you planning to do, Crow?

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:38.100
When this effect Special Summons Zephyros 
the Elite, I can set a card to destroy it!

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:45.640
Since I set a card, Crimson Mefist's effect 
deals damage, but Damage Drain negates it!

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:54.440
Once again, I return a card to my hand 
to Special Summon Zephyros the Elite!

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:03.370
Then I set a card to destroy Zephyros!

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:10.300
Black-Winged Dragon's 
wings are turning black!

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:13.630
Yeah.  It's using its own body as a shield.

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:16.440
The pain shaves away its body.

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:23.960
Bolger, you should've known that Pearson 
wanted to do more than build a D-Wheel.

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:28.720
He wanted the kids to learn 
that they could do anything

00:18:28.720 --> 00:18:32.950
without having to rely on the City's power!

00:18:32.950 --> 00:18:35.560
That's why Pearson refused their help!

00:18:40.230 --> 00:18:45.200
Did I have a misunderstanding?

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:48.170
That's right!  Remember what Pearson said!

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:52.710
I know how they feel.

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:56.780
The pain of losing your parents,

00:18:56.780 --> 00:19:01.740
having no place to go and not 
knowing why you were even born.

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:09.020
Black-Winged Dragon absorbs 
the pain to darken its wings!

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:11.800
This dragon is the same as Pearson!

00:19:13.530 --> 00:19:17.480
He carried the burden of 
Satellite's sadness and pain!

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:23.590
Pearson wanted to free Satellite by 
building Satellite's first-ever D-Wheel!

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:25.870
That's why...

00:19:27.920 --> 00:19:32.240
Black-Winged Dragon flew down to Pearson!

00:19:33.170 --> 00:19:36.180
Black-Winged Dragon is completely black!

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:40.350
Bolger!

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:47.890
Black-Winged Dragon's black wings are 
the pain Pearson received from you!

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:50.470
Feel the same pain!

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:53.870
I activate Black-Winged Dragon's effect!

00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:58.190
Once per turn, I return the amount of attack 
points it lost due to this card's effect...

00:19:58.190 --> 00:20:03.270
...and all your monsters' attack 
points decrease by that amount!

00:20:03.610 --> 00:20:04.980
Black Burst!

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:19.190
While Black-Winged Dragon was absorbing 
pain, it was storing power.

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:23.030
Black-Winged Dragon attacks Crimson Mefist!

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:25.820
Noble Stream!

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:41.080
Hooray!  Crow won!

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:43.780
You did it, Crow.

00:20:58.500 --> 00:20:59.580
Pearson...

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:04.810
You really cared about the kids.

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:09.480
I was the one blinded by fame, not you.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:11.610
I'm sorry.

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:16.340
Bolger...

00:21:25.830 --> 00:21:28.860
Pearson, Bolger turned himself in.

00:21:29.490 --> 00:21:32.070
Your feelings touched him.

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:35.100
Black-Winged Dragon...

00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:37.880
I'll continue your legacy!

00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:41.190
Pearson...

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:13.250
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:13.250 --> 00:22:18.130
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:18.130 --> 00:22:23.070
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:28.080
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:33.130
The cruel god tests us

00:22:33.130 --> 00:22:39.690
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:39.690 --> 00:22:43.760
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:49.600
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:49.600 --> 00:22:53.690
Bond is the proper word

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:59.310
As we fight, we understand each other

00:22:59.310 --> 00:23:02.490
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:02.490 --> 00:23:04.750
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:04.750 --> 00:23:09.280
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:12.250
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:12.250 --> 00:23:15.690
You want to party until the morning

00:23:15.690 --> 00:23:19.070
At our special place
